    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d66b6d2a_fdc4feaf",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 50
      },
      "lineNbr": 495,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-10T13:14:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If CS always checks the bpf map contents from handler thread, we will have race issue.\nFor example, if the the following two operations happens in a short second\n1. uid0 register network request\n2. Update firewall0 to deny uid0 (this is done in binder thread)\n2. Update firewall1 to deny uid0 (this is done in binder thread)\n\nWe need to send callback in the order of BLOCKED_REASON_NONE -\u003e BLOCKED_REASON_CHAIN0 -\u003e BLOCKED_REASON_CHAIN0+1.\nBut, without maintaining states in CS, it would be difficult to send blocked status callback correctly from handler thread.\n\nFor example, if we check the bpf contents while processing register network request event from handler thread, bpf might already have firewall0 and firewall1 rule for uid0.\n\nAlso, reusing EVENT_UIDS_BLOCKED_REASONS_CHANGED makes this CL simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "a9b83b2e_0b719c45",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 495,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 495,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "809acd45be0f85761c7beb21226fb9553333f572",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
